{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "03122",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.78,
      "end_seconds": 4.96,
      "duration_seconds": 4.18,
      "text": "Hi, doctor, I hope I'm not disturbing you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 6.01,
      "end_seconds": 9.75,
      "duration_seconds": 3.74,
      "text": "No problem at all, come in. What's troubling you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 11.47,
      "end_seconds": 17.15,
      "duration_seconds": 5.68,
      "text": "Good afternoon, doctor. I look after them so I thought I'd come."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 18.95,
      "end_seconds": 22.58,
      "duration_seconds": 3.63,
      "text": "Good, that'll be useful. Pull up a chair."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 24.22,
      "end_seconds": 39.5,
      "duration_seconds": 15.28,
      "text": "So, I've been feeling very weak, doctor. I'm not great at remembering details, so bear with me. I'd rather not end up on lots of tablets if I can avoid it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 41.55,
      "end_seconds": 42.82,
      "duration_seconds": 1.27,
      "text": "Since when exactly?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 44.71,
      "end_seconds": 48.95,
      "duration_seconds": 4.24,
      "text": "It's been going on for about two weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 49.68,
      "end_seconds": 52.95,
      "duration_seconds": 3.27,
      "text": "How troublesome is it day to day?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 54.96,
      "end_seconds": 57.69,
      "duration_seconds": 2.73,
      "text": "It feels moderate to me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 59.75,
      "end_seconds": 63.68,
      "duration_seconds": 3.93,
      "text": "What about shaking chills, have you noticed that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 65.48,
      "end_seconds": 67.79,
      "duration_seconds": 2.31,
      "text": "Yes, for three days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 69.75,
      "end_seconds": 72.62,
      "duration_seconds": 2.87,
      "text": "How often do you get it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 73.19,
      "end_seconds": 79.99,
      "duration_seconds": 6.8,
      "text": "I'd say a few times a day. There's a high temperature as well."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 81.83,
      "end_seconds": 85.33,
      "duration_seconds": 3.5,
      "text": "Rate it for me, mild, moderate or severe?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 86.96,
      "end_seconds": 89.67,
      "duration_seconds": 2.71,
      "text": "It feels moderate to me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 91.05,
      "end_seconds": 93.98,
      "duration_seconds": 2.93,
      "text": "Have you had a sore mouth?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 96.73,
      "end_seconds": 99.19,
      "duration_seconds": 2.46,
      "text": "Yeah. Ten days, I'd say."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 100.25,
      "end_seconds": 103.0,
      "duration_seconds": 2.75,
      "text": "And what about rash or diarrhoea?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 103.73,
      "end_seconds": 106.49,
      "duration_seconds": 2.76,
      "text": "No, nothing to report there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 108.49,
      "end_seconds": 110.61,
      "duration_seconds": 2.12,
      "text": "And cough, any of that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 111.85,
      "end_seconds": 113.61,
      "duration_seconds": 1.76,
      "text": "No cough, thankfully."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 114.51,
      "end_seconds": 120.55,
      "duration_seconds": 6.04,
      "text": "Actually, you know, doctor, I did notice cough. She doesn't always say."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 124.83,
      "end_seconds": 130.44,
      "duration_seconds": 5.61,
      "text": "No, I don't think I did. Maybe a little, I'm not sure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 134.99,
      "end_seconds": 141.79,
      "duration_seconds": 6.8,
      "text": "Alright, I'll note both what you've said and what you've noticed. Anything unusual with passing urine?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 143.29,
      "end_seconds": 144.85,
      "duration_seconds": 1.56,
      "text": "No changes there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 146.33,
      "end_seconds": 149.59,
      "duration_seconds": 3.26,
      "text": "Okay, now some background about your lifestyle."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 150.17,
      "end_seconds": 162.91,
      "duration_seconds": 12.74,
      "text": "I only drink at family occasions. I have about eight cigarettes in a day. My partner and our baby. I retired from the post office two years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 164.25,
      "end_seconds": 169.34,
      "duration_seconds": 5.09,
      "text": "Can you list what you take, tablets, creams or inhalers?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 169.97,
      "end_seconds": 176.04,
      "duration_seconds": 6.07,
      "text": "I take aspirin, 75 milligrams, once a day for my heart."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 177.55,
      "end_seconds": 187.46,
      "duration_seconds": 9.91,
      "text": "So, you know, doctor, I think the last prescription for the aspirin was 150 milligrams. We changed it at the last visit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 188.9,
      "end_seconds": 193.27,
      "duration_seconds": 4.37,
      "text": "Hm, that's different. Is the latest prescription anywhere near you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 194.37,
      "end_seconds": 208.7,
      "duration_seconds": 14.33,
      "text": "No, I left it at home. I'm on metoprolol, 50 milligrams, twice a day. It's chemotherapy last week, recent. Before this I was on warfarin; that's been stopped."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 209.77,
      "end_seconds": 212.31,
      "duration_seconds": 2.54,
      "text": "Have you had any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 212.82,
      "end_seconds": 214.49,
      "duration_seconds": 1.67,
      "text": "No surgery, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 215.69,
      "end_seconds": 219.25,
      "duration_seconds": 3.56,
      "text": "Anything in your past medical history I should know?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 222.89,
      "end_seconds": 233.11,
      "duration_seconds": 10.22,
      "text": "Erm, you know, I've had heart disease for about a year now. I, I have an irregular heartbeat."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 235.07,
      "end_seconds": 241.93,
      "duration_seconds": 6.86,
      "text": "Okay, I can see heart disease and an irregular heartbeat in your file as well."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 252.0,
      "end_seconds": 259.82,
      "duration_seconds": 7.82,
      "text": "Has anything ever caused you a reaction? I mean any allergies. Just so I get the full picture."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 265.41,
      "end_seconds": 268.46,
      "duration_seconds": 3.05,
      "text": "No, I'm not allergic to anything."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 269.68,
      "end_seconds": 272.8,
      "duration_seconds": 3.12,
      "text": "Are there any illnesses in your family?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 275.42,
      "end_seconds": 280.95,
      "duration_seconds": 5.53,
      "text": "My father has Parkinson's disease. My mother had a stroke."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 282.33,
      "end_seconds": 284.71,
      "duration_seconds": 2.38,
      "text": "Let me take your readings now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 290.91,
      "end_seconds": 293.16,
      "duration_seconds": 2.25,
      "text": "Nearly done with the readings..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 304.07,
      "end_seconds": 319.1,
      "duration_seconds": 15.03,
      "text": "Okay: pulse is 99 beats a minute, pressure 102 over 58, weight 77 kilos, oxygen saturation is 98 percent, BMI works out to 25.1, temperature 37.1, height 175 centimetres."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 320.7,
      "end_seconds": 322.35,
      "duration_seconds": 1.65,
      "text": "Is that normal?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 323.57,
      "end_seconds": 326.52,
      "duration_seconds": 2.95,
      "text": "We'll look at it together shortly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 327.64,
      "end_seconds": 331.34,
      "duration_seconds": 3.7,
      "text": "Let me look at the area, I'll be gentle."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 333.24,
      "end_seconds": 335.33,
      "duration_seconds": 2.09,
      "text": "Hold that for a second."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 347.04,
      "end_seconds": 355.29,
      "duration_seconds": 8.25,
      "text": "You are hot, shaking and your blood pressure is low, and you had chemotherapy nine days ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 360.21,
      "end_seconds": 362.04,
      "duration_seconds": 1.83,
      "text": "You can relax now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 370.62,
      "end_seconds": 395.56,
      "duration_seconds": 24.94,
      "text": "From what you've told me and what I found, it points towards neutropenic sepsis. I want to be honest that this is an impression, not a final answer. We shouldn't forget a chest infection. So, to recap quickly. You've been feeling very weak for about two weeks, moderate, and no diarrhoea or rash."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 396.45,
      "end_seconds": 397.97,
      "duration_seconds": 1.52,
      "text": "That's it, yes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 411.4,
      "end_seconds": 416.61,
      "duration_seconds": 5.21,
      "text": "Urgent blood tests is what I'd like next, for neutropenic sepsis."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 422.11,
      "end_seconds": 423.94,
      "duration_seconds": 1.83,
      "text": "That's fine with me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 425.63,
      "end_seconds": 462.13,
      "duration_seconds": 36.5,
      "text": "For this, piperacillin and tazobactam, 4.5 grams, now, single dose. It's for neutropenic sepsis. This is an emergency, antibiotics are being given within the hour. And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose. If the symptoms get worse, that's the point to come in urgently. Please come and see me straight away. Let me check I've been clear. What will you do once you get home?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 462.64,
      "end_seconds": 474.04,
      "duration_seconds": 11.4,
      "text": "So, you know, I take the piperacillin and tazobactam, 4.5 grams, now and come back straight away. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0057",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 475.02,
      "end_seconds": 479.49,
      "duration_seconds": 4.47,
      "text": "Yes, exactly right. So, that's all from me. Any questions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0058",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 480.99,
      "end_seconds": 484.02,
      "duration_seconds": 3.03,
      "text": "I think I understand everything. Thanks."
    }
  ]
}